OK, I recall someone mentioning this exact same thing once before...
but now I've experienced the same thing... and for all intents and
purposes, believe this should be considered a bug.

On the Samurai quest, make it down to the last level, wander
up to the quest nemisis, hit him two times before he wakes up
(due to speed + boots, I suppose) and he teleports away...
BEFORE EVER PICKING UP THE TSURAGI. So I just hop on it. Pick
it up, wield it, and proceed to beat him up with it.

Now, on other quests, I've noticed the quest nemisis picks up
the quest object as soon as he/she/it awakens, but never thought
much of it.

Seems to me, you could simply zap them with a teleport wand, before
they ever picked it up, and nab it straight off.

Someone should really fix it so they have it from the get go, to
avoid this sort of thing.

